  "id": "farmer-carry",
  "name": "Farmer Carry",
  "definition": "A duration-tracked bilateral dumbbell carry in which equal implements create a continuous tendency to open both hands while the athlete walks forward on a level surface with the upper arms at the sides, neutral humeral and forearm rotation, the elbows held extended, and no grip assistance. The sagittal family plane is grounded in resisted hand.fingerExtension. Ordinary gait remains the locomotor substrate rather than a set of training-defining prime actions. Ellestad, McGill, and Stastny directly support balanced bilateral carriage, the trunk-control envelope, and the reviewed lower-limb control surfaces. Loaded-grip, upper-limb, and soleus assignments not measured by those panels are explicitly anatomy-and-mechanics-derived. Holds, suitcase carriage, marching in place, backward or turning paths, uneven paired loads, straps, trap bars, rack, overhead, front-loaded, yoke, and lunge variants remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine",
    "gaffney-2014-trapezius-subdivisions",
    "holzbaur-2005-upper-extremity",
    "mirakhorlo-2018-hand-wrist-model",
    "ellestad-2024-loaded-carry-muscle-activation",
    "mcgill-2013-one-two-hand-carry",
    "stastny-2015-farmers-walk-lower-limb"
  ],
